---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data';

const resumePdf = '/downloads/resume-testdevelop.pdf';
---
<BaseLayout title="Resume — wujue / Dithob" description="wujue / Dithob online resume: AI applications, agent tooling, and test development, with verifiable evidence." lang="en" path="/en/resume/">
  <div class="page-intro shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">Resume</div>
    <h1>Online resume</h1>
    <p>CS graduate student focused on AI applications, agent tooling, and test development. Every item below traces back to a public repository or verifiable source.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={resumePdf} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download PDF resume ↓</a>
      <a class="button" href={`mailto:${site.mail}`}>Email me ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section shell content-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Profile</h2>
      <p>CS student working on AI applications, agent tooling, RAG/OCR, document understanding, and engineering quality. I like turning ideas into tools that run, can be checked, and state their boundaries honestly — with hands-on experience shipping AI test agents from case generation to self-healing loops.</p>

      <h2>Internship</h2>
      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-entry-heading"><h3>Test Development Intern</h3><span class="resume-org">Tencent Cloud & Smart Industries</span><span class="resume-entry-date">2026.06 – 2026.09</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Mobile Maps UI Automation Testing Agent</strong>: contributed to the Tencent Maps UI automation platform, owning agent orchestration plus Skill and MCP tool rollout across 17 business domains and 600+ test cases.</li>
          <li><strong>Multi-agent cross-checking & Skill evaluation</strong>: produced 85 graded cases via independent multi-agent generation, cross-comparison, and merge, closed with human review in an "AI-generated + human-judged" loop; planned 120 evaluation cases for map-query and map-rendering Skills and codified the Agent/Skill evaluation methodology.</li>
          <li><strong>Release requirement testing</strong>: drove test analysis for the "You use, we compensate" H5 release, identifying cross-day state machines, re-entry, out-of-app sharing, analytics, and compatibility risks into an R1–R8 risk register aligned with product and developers; authored cases per internal platform standards and built self-test plans for developers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-entry-heading"><h3>Intelligent Continuous Testing Platform</h3><span class="resume-org">Solo design & development</span><span class="resume-entry-date">2025.10 – 2026.02</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Platform & framework design</strong>: built a five-layer API automation framework with Python/Pytest/Requests, auto-generated contract cases from OpenAPI validating status codes, response schemas, and business error codes; assembled a lightweight platform on Vue.js + FastAPI + MySQL + Redis + Docker to manage projects and cases.</li>
          <li><strong>UI automation & performance testing</strong>: implemented Playwright PO-pattern business cases with Trace, screenshots, and recording for replay; designed ramp-up, stability, and peak load tests with JMeter/Locust, reporting QPS, P95, and error rates while locating slow endpoints.</li>
          <li><strong>AI enhancement & quality loop</strong>: wrapped Pytest/Playwright/Locust execution as async Redis-queued platform tasks; introduced an LLM case-generation pipeline (draft → human review → Bad Case retention); report pages aggregate pass rates, failure reasons, and trends into a closed loop.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-entry-heading"><h3>Tencent Maps UI Automation Testing Agent</h3><span class="resume-org">Framework team contributor</span><span class="resume-entry-date">2026.06 – 2026.09</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Agent orchestration & case generation</strong>: co-built the agentic test system orchestrating 13 Skills and 3 in-house MCP services from requirement understanding to targeted regression across 17 business domains and 600+ cases; linked TAPD/Figma to auto-generate executable case.py, ~10–15 min per case versus 1–2 hours handwritten.</li>
          <li><strong>MCP tooling & multimodal perception</strong>: developed device-control and failure-diagnosis MCP tools and integrated a maps MCP resolving coordinates; fused UIAutomator, OCR, OmniParser, and OpenCV with chained fallback for self-drawn widgets lacking resource-id; scrcpy projection cut screenshot latency from 1s to 30–100ms.</li>
          <li><strong>Knowledge engineering & semantic retrieval</strong>: designed a file-based knowledge graph (Page/Component/Pitfall/Operation nodes) with static reasoning over UI indexes from 23 developer repos so the agent reads dev code before writing cases; AST-scanned 1500+ private helpers and reused them via jieba + BM25 semantic retrieval.</li>
          <li><strong>Reliability & self-healing loop</strong>: guarded generation with intent locking, nine-dimension self-review, and human takeover; enforced Lint gates and step-wise assertions, pruned flaky cases via health backtest pass rates, and auto-regenerated patches from evidence packages after failures.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Academic highlights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Competitions</strong>: Silver, 2025 "Internet+" Innovation & Entrepreneurship Competition; university second prize, China International College Students' Innovation Competition; provincial third prize, Chongqing AI Large Model Innovation Application Competition.</li>
        <li><strong>Paper</strong>: "LHAF: A Lightweight Hierarchical Adaptive Framework for LLM-based Multimodal Emotion Recognition in Conversations" (submitted to SCI Q1).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Test development</strong>: equivalence partitioning, boundary value, scenario, state-machine, and decision-table design; full test lifecycle from requirement review through regression; TAPD and internal case/defect platforms.</li>
        <li><strong>Engineering & tooling</strong>: API automation with Python/Pytest/Requests; UI/mobile automation with Playwright, Selenium, uiautomator2, and ADB; load testing with JMeter and Locust; Linux, FastAPI, MySQL, Docker, Git.</li>
        <li><strong>AI application & testing</strong>: understands RAG, Harness, and Memory agent mechanics; fluent in MCP, Skill, and Subagent frameworks; builds Golden Dataset and Bad Case feedback loops with hallucination, refusal, formatting, and multi-turn regression suites validated by keyword, JSON Schema, similarity, and rule assertions; production experience in auto-updating agent cases with human review.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Education</h2>
      <div class="resume-entry">
        <div class="resume-entry-heading"><h3>Chongqing University of Posts and Telecommunications · Computer Technology (M.Sc.)</h3><span class="resume-entry-date">2024.09 – 2027.06</span></div>
        <ul><li>Top-tier academic scholarship ×1; second-tier ×1.</li></ul>
        <div class="resume-entry-heading"><h3>Chongqing University of Posts and Telecommunications · Computer Science (B.Sc.)</h3><span class="resume-entry-date">2020.09 – 2024.07</span></div>
        <ul><li>Third-tier academic scholarship; GPA 3.28/4.0 (top 25% of major).</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>GitHub</dt><dd><a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">github.com/Dithob</a></dd>
      <dt>Email</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${site.mail}`}>{site.mail}</a></dd>
      <dt>PDF resume</dt><dd><a href={resumePdf} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">resume-testdevelop.pdf ↓</a></dd>
      <dt>Education</dt><dd>Chongqing University of Posts and Telecommunications · Computer Technology (M.Sc.)</dd>
      <dt>Focus</dt><dd>AI Applications / Agent Tooling / Test Development</dd>
      <dt>Public entry</dt><dd><a href="/en/projects/">Projects and evidence →</a> · <a href="/en/notes/">Notes →</a></dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
